    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Sets project parameters in one or more Omniscope projects: each input record gives a project's address and the values for parameters named like its fields.",
    "category": "Preparation",
    "subcategory": "Workflow",
    "tags": [
        "parameter",
        "project parameters",
        "batch",
        "for each",
        "rest api",
        "orchestration"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "For each input record, sets parameters of the project whose address is in the record. A field named like a parameter sets that parameter: a field *Region* holding *North* sets the parameter *Region* to *North*.\n\n**Setting up**\n\n1. Choose the field holding the project addresses, ending in .iox, for example `http://127.0.0.1:24679/Folder/Project.iox/`.\n2. Choose the parameter fields.\n\nRecords are applied in order, so when two records name the same project, the later one's values stay. Each record's values are set together or not at all. The user needs the *Project parameters access via APIs* permission. The input records are passed on unchanged.",
    "dependencies": "urllib3",
    "options": [
        {
            "name": "Iox_File_Url",
            "title": "Project address field",
            "description": "The field holding each record's project address, ending in .iox. On the same server, the internal address such as http://127.0.0.1:24679/Folder/Project.iox/ avoids the public address and its certificate. A report or workflow address of the project is cut back to the project.",
            "groupTitle": "Projects",
            "width": "ONE",
